# API Python

## Module ownership (one home per concern)

| Area | Owns |
| ---- | ---- |
| `main.py` | Routes, middleware, lifespan |
| `agent.py` / `brain.py` | Turn orchestration, model routing |
| `tools/` | Tool registry and side-effect-free reads |
| `connectors/` | Gmail, calendar, Drive, Sheets, search |
| `hermes/` | Gateway bridge, MCP, playbooks |
| `quote.py`, `rfq.py`, `cnc_suggest.py` | Shop workflows (see domain rules) |
| `memory/` | Local RAG store (SQLite + LanceDB under `data/memory/`) |
| `db.py`, `schemas.py` | Schema and migrations (see `12-data-schema`) |
| `config.py` | **`Settings` only** — no parallel env readers |

## Conventions

- **Config:** read paths, keys, and ports from `settings` (`app.config`); anchor relative dirs via repo root, not process CWD.
- **Lazy imports:** import heavy connectors and model clients inside the function that needs them; avoid new top-level import cycles.
- **No new JSON state files** for durable data — SQLite tables or documented exports only.
- **External I/O:** every HTTP/RPC call to Hermes, Gemini, Ollama, Voicebox, or Google APIs must use an explicit timeout; no unbounded `wait`.
- **Extend, don't fork:** new features hook existing modules; no parallel stack under `backend/`.

Skills carry long procedures; this file states only break-if-wrong constraints.
